    "number": 131,
    "title": "Track Pixoo monitoring packaging and pending acceptance",
    "body": "Pixoo #34 now has a source packaging candidate at https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/pull/65. Refresh the shared guide's backlog and remaining-work narrative to show that work while retaining installation, client, physical and Hub #6 frontend gates.\n\nThe same delivery coordinator owns both PRs. This guide candidate records source work in progress, not a predicted merge or issue closure. A completion reconciliation will record the actual source result. No architecture ownership or command flow changes, so no diagram redraw is needed. Public publication remains outside scope.\n\nValidation: guide generation, all five maintenance tests, generated-output no-drift check and browser/print checks pass. HTML SHA-256: a81b5e245e1e4dbc2ad0653e190723443fb52ece911706df507203802bb868df. Browser checks cover six widths, links, controls, nine companion viewers and print restoration, with no errors.\n\nGuide-only CI receipt: base 012de557257940cc66913c64012cf4d85e13fb91; all six changed paths are under docs/work-guide/. Both unchanged workflow triggers exclude that directory for pull_request and main push. Independent Standards and Specification review, provider readbacks and guarded merge remain required. Protection reads return the account-plan HTTP 403; repository procedural gates remain in force.\n",
    "state": "open",
